{
 "plan": {
  "title": "District Health Profile",
  "subtitle": "Comparative analysis of key health and nutrition indicators across districts",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Districts Surveyed",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"District\") AS n FROM district_health_factsheet",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Avg. Stunting Rate",
    "sql": "SELECT AVG(\"Children under 5 years who are stunted (%)\") AS n FROM district_health_factsheet",
    "unit": "%"
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Vaccination vs. Institutional Births by District",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", AVG(\"Children age 12-23 months fully vaccinated (%)\") AS vaccination, AVG(\"Institutional births (%)\") AS births FROM district_health_factsheet GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
    "x": "District",
    "y": [
     "vaccination",
     "births"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Sanitation and Literacy Rates",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", AVG(\"Households with improved sanitation facility (%)\") AS sanitation, AVG(\"Women age 15-49 years who are literate (%)\") AS literacy FROM district_health_factsheet GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
    "x": "District",
    "y": [
     "sanitation",
     "literacy"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Detailed District Health Metrics",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", \"State\", AVG(\"Children age 12-23 months fully vaccinated (%)\") AS avg_vaccination, AVG(\"Children under 5 years who are stunted (%)\") AS avg_stunting, AVG(\"Households with improved sanitation facility (%)\") AS avg_sanitation FROM district_health_factsheet GROUP BY 1, 2 ORDER BY 1"
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "The health landscape across the {{p1.n}} surveyed districts shows a varying level of coverage. The average stunting rate across all regions is recorded at {{p2.n}}%.\n\nComparing vaccination rates and institutional births reveals significant disparities between districts. While some areas show high levels of {{p3.vaccination}}, others lag in essential services. \n\nFurthermore, the correlation between literacy levels and sanitation access is visible in the regional trends. The data suggests that districts with higher literacy {{p4.literacy}} often align with improved sanitation facilities {{p4.sanitation}}."
 },
